{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"2205","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Simons and Cakes for Success"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"When I succeed, we'll share the cakes together!"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"— SHUN"}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Simons has $$$n$$$ friends and a huge amount of cakes. To divide the cakes fairly, you are asked to help him solve the following problem:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Find the minimum "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"positive"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integer $$$k$$$ such that $$$n$$$ is a divisor of $$$k^n$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proved that the answer always exists under the given constraints."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 100$$$). The description of the test cases follows. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The only line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$2\\le n\\le 10^9$$$) — the number of friends Simons has."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output a single integer — the minimum $$$k$$$ you found."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n8\n12\n369\n55635800\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n2\n6\n123\n2090\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1^8=1$$$, and $$$8$$$ is not a divisor of $$$1$$$; "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2^8=256$$$, and $$$8$$$ is a divisor of $$$256$$$, because $$$256 = 8\\cdot 32$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Thus, the minimum possible $$$k$$$ is $$$2$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, $$$12$$$ is a divisor of $$$6^{12}=2\\,176\\,782\\,336$$$, because $$$2\\,176\\,782\\,336=12\\cdot 181\\,398\\,528$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"2205B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/2205/problem/B"}